@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Mixed MVP / future. Retained broader-product associations require explicit future node labels; MVP uses only core/basic ProjectForge.
title MVP + EXPLICIT FUTURE PATHS — Resumefolio — selected UML use-case scope (existing UC-D bundles)
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 190

left to right direction
actor "Private user" as U
actor "Employer viewer" as E
actor "Scoped collaborator" as C
actor "Authorized operator" as O
rectangle Resumefolio {
 usecase "UC-D01\nTailor independent resumes" as U1
 usecase "UC-D02\nConfigure PDF / sharing controls" as U2
 usecase "UC-D03\nView selected protected material" as U3
 usecase "UC-D04\nPrepare manual application / progress" as U4
 usecase "UC-D05\nPreserve actual submitted material" as U5
 usecase "UC-D06\nCoordinate authorized mail / calendar" as U6
 usecase "UC-D07\n[AFTER MVP] Refine work / coherent Sprint plan" as U7
 usecase "UC-D08\nAccept scoped collaboration / changed access" as U8
 usecase "UC-D09\nUse real Git / current review" as U9
 usecase "UC-D10\nGated execution / separate target stage" as U10
 usecase "UC-D11\nManage effective policy / evidence" as U11
 usecase "UC-D12\nRestore and reconcile access / effects" as U12
}
U --> U1
U --> U2
E --> U3
U --> U4
U --> U5
U --> U6
C --> U7
C --> U8
C --> U9
U --> U10
O --> U11
O --> U12
legend bottom
 Overview associations do not allocate final roles or require automatic side effects.
 Exact actor/action policy and operation-level use cases remain in the source catalog.
endlegend
@enduml
